 Scholar ] 19. Powell L, Andrzejowski J, Taylor R et al. Comparison of the performance of four laryngoscopes in a high-fidelity simulator using normal and difficult airway. Br J Anaesth 2009;103:755–60. 10.1093/bja/aep232 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Cavus E, Callies A, Doerges V et al. The C-MAC videolaryngoscope for prehospital emergency intubation: a prospective, multicentre, observational study. Emerg Med J 2011;28:650–3. 10.1136/emj.2010.098707 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Hodd JA, Doyle DJ, Gupta S et al. A Mannequin study of intubation with the AP advance and GlideScope Ranger videolaryngoscopes and the Macintosh laryngoscope. Anesth Analg 2011;113:791–800. 10.1213/ANE.0b013e3182288bda [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Schälte G, Scheid U, Rex S et al. The use of the Airtraq® optical laryngoscope for routine tracheal intubation in high-risk cardio-surgical patients. BMC Res Notes 2011;4:425 10.1186/1756-0500-4-425 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Claret PG, Bobbia X, Asencio R et al. Comparison of the Airtraq laryngoscope versus the conventional Macintosh laryngoscope while wearing CBRN-PPE. Eur J Emerg Med 2016;23:119–23. 10.1097/MEJ.0000000000000220 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Nakstad AR, Sandberg M. Airway management in simulated restricted access to a patient—can manikin-based studies provide relevant data? Scand J Trauma Resusc Emerg Med 2011;19:36 10.1186/1757-7241-19-36 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Apfelbaum JL, Hagberg CA, Caplan RA et al. , American Society of Anesthesiologists Task Force on Management of the Difficult Airway. Practice guidelines for management of the difficult airway: an updated report by the American Society of Anesthesiologists Task Force on Management of the Difficult Airway. Anesthesiology 2013;118:251–70. 10.1097/ALN.0b013e31827773b2 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]',6,'2025-10-15 11:02:37','2025-10-15 11:02:37')